From 4de2a797ef0b59d0623c4bea15d56012515b495d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HempFiend <17104973+jaidenscool1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 23:43:09 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Blaze 3.x: OSDKSettings (2249) gets NHL 15 to its online
 menus

Component 0x08C9 is Blaze::OSDKSettings (fetchSettings = 1, fetchSettingsGroups = 2), not
OsdkTicker2. NHL 15 builds its settings groups, views and settings from these replies and looks
them up by name with no null check: the empty replies crashed it at 0x008b1aec (ticker group
O_SG_TCKR), then 0x7a2840/0x7a2878 (account settings O_SPAMEA/O_SPAMPART in view UACCT).

Serve the five groups the game names (O_SG_NRAD/QMSG/SYSS/TCKR/USER) with the TDF tags read from
the EBOOT's member tables, the ticker's integer settings (O_TKfriend/O_TKsport/O_TKfilter),
O_SG_USER's views (MUPSET/INV/UGEN/UACCT) and the two account settings. The matchmaking settings
(O_JS, O_GM, O_MIN, ...) are created by the game itself; serving them too corrupts its settings
manager (0x828b88). With the RPCS3 built-in patch for the dynamic-message rotation (uscl-rpcs3 0012)
NHL reaches the main menu and the online hub; next is the roster check. See
docs/EA-Sports-Blaze3-heat2.md section 6.

